  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the key uncertainty is whether a well-motivated multimodal configuration can achieve strong validation accuracy, and which component choices matter most. config_009 (multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, resnet50, weighted fusion) tests a strong, standard multimodal setup: a learned RNA encoder (scgpt) that should capture nonlinear biological signal better than PCA, a well-validated image encoder (resnet50), and a simple robust weighted fusion. This is the best first experiment because it establishes a high-quality reference point in the multimodal space with minimal architectural complexity (singleprofile, no aggregation step), making it easier to diagnose which axis to push next (multiprofile, transformer aggregation, ViT-L image encoder, concat fusion, scvi_n200) if performance is promising, or to identify a weak modality if it underperforms."
}

